      <data key="d0">Qwen3-4B</data>
      <data key="d1">model</data>
      <data key="d2">Qwen3-4B is a backbone model employed in the evaluation of question answering methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Qwen3-4B serves as the backbone model used in the experiments conducted with TagRAG.&lt;SEP&gt;Qwen3-4B is a language model used in experiments comparing TagRAG's performance against different configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Qwen3-4B is a model referenced in performance evaluations of TagRAG against various baselines across different datasets.&lt;SEP&gt;Qwen3-4B is a more extensive model compared to Qwen3-1.7B used in the analysis of lightweight adaptation.&lt;SEP&gt;Qwen3-4B is a model or system referenced in the context of feature selection techniques evaluation between TagRAG and NaiveRAG.&lt;SEP&gt;Qwen3-4B is a model or system referenced in evaluations of TagTAG and GraphRAG, providing context for feature selection methodologies.</data>
