    <node id="HippoRAG2">
      <data key="d0">HippoRAG2</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">HippoRAG2 is a baseline retrieval method that achieves high coverage but may struggle with leading positions for critical documents.&lt;SEP&gt;HippoRAG2 is one of the backbone models used in the iterative retrieval study within GraphRAG.&lt;SEP&gt;HippoRAG2 is a retrieval method based on PPR that integrates with various GraphRAG variants.&lt;SEP&gt;HippoRAG2 is a technique that uses personalized PageRank for improving entity retrieval in question answering.&lt;SEP&gt;HippoRAG2 is a retrieval method used as a benchmark for comparison against other information retrieval techniques.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbcf5df5b02a500f3b2ea2c8ec7025cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd16cb2c8cbacbc8139b2f74a3aae2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RAPTOR">
      <data key="d0">RAPTOR</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">RAPTOR is a retrieval method discussed in the context of its performance in multi-hop reasoning tasks and its challenges with recall.&lt;SEP&gt;RAPTOR is another backbone model integrated into the GraphRAG framework for the study of iterative retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;RAPTOR is a tree-based retrieval method discussed in the context of performance evaluation of multi-hop QA.&lt;SEP&gt;RAPTOR is a tree-based hierarchical organization method designed to summarize evidence effectively in retrieval tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;RAPTOR is a retrieval method evaluated in the context of the ablation study, providing base performance metrics for comparison with enhancements.&lt;SEP&gt;RAPTOR is a dataset-based method intended for recursive text chunk inference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbcf5df5b02a500f3b2ea2c8ec7025cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6323519fa42575408756a46a90ad82c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd16cb2c8cbacbc8139b2f74a3aae2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GFM-RAG">
      <data key="d0">GFM-RAG</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">GFM-RAG is a GNN-based retrieval method included in the analysis of various frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;GFM-RAG is a specific system that explores iterative retrieval approaches in the context of GraphRAG.&lt;SEP&gt;GFM-RAG employs graph neural networks to encode relationships and enhance multi-hop reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a18be2a653ce076549457febaf41543</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="IRCOT">
      <data key="d0">IRCOT</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">IRCOT is a retrieval strategy evaluated for its effectiveness in enhancing performance on complex multi-hop questions.&lt;SEP&gt;IRCOT is an iterative retrieval strategy that has been identified to improve the performance by surfacing missing bridge evidence.&lt;SEP&gt;IRCOT is a method that combines iterative retrieval with reasoning processes for improved evidence acquisition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbcf5df5b02a500f3b2ea2c8ec7025cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cda1598277a8b2328ba59179c044b1e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="IRGS">
      <data key="d0">IRGS</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">IRGS is another retrieval strategy assessed alongside IRCOT, noted for its complementary strengths in information retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;IRGS is another iterative retrieval strategy that is compared for its effectiveness in capturing distinct aspects of evidence.&lt;SEP&gt;IRGS is an iterative retrieval strategy that is compared against the BDTR framework in the evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;IRGS emphasizes the integration of retrieval and generation for enhanced evidence grounding.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbcf5df5b02a500f3b2ea2c8ec7025cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cda1598277a8b2328ba59179c044b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe13b92a1c768e1d7f7a8b32dd7be5d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TOG">
      <data key="d0">TOG</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">TOG is another iterative retrieval strategy that is evaluated against BDTR.&lt;SEP&gt;TOG extends iterative retrieval techniques to graph models for comprehensive reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe13b92a1c768e1d7f7a8b32dd7be5d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GCOT">
      <data key="d0">GCOT</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">GCOT is yet another iterative retrieval strategy used for comparison in the evaluations of BDTR.&lt;SEP&gt;GCOT integrates graph structures within the chain-of-thought framework for effective multi-hop reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe13b92a1c768e1d7f7a8b32dd7be5d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BDTR">
      <data key="d0">BDTR</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">BDTR, or Bridge-Guided Dual-Thought-based Retrieval, is a framework that targets bottlenecks in GraphRAG by generating dual thoughts at reasoning steps for improved retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;BDTR stands for Bridge-Guided Dual-Thought-based Retrieval, a framework proposed to improve performance in multi-hop question answering.&lt;SEP&gt;BDTR stands for Bridge-Guided Dual-Thought-based Retrieval, which combines retrieval strategies for improved outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;BDTR is a combined retrieval method that utilizes both Dual-Thought-Based Retrieval and Bridge-Guided Evidence Calibration for optimal performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd16cb2c8cbacbc8139b2f74a3aae2c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe13b92a1c768e1d7f7a8b32dd7be5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cda1598277a8b2328ba59179c044b1e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MiniRAG">
      <data key="d0">MiniRAG</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">MiniRAG is a method developed by Fan et al. in 2025 that retrieves relevant subgraphs to generate fine-grained answers in inference tasks. It integrates text and entity indexing into a semantic-aware graph, enhancing search efficiency and facilitating effective knowledge discovery. This method achieves high efficiency, particularly for small language models, through its semantic-aware graph indexing and lightweight topology-based retrieval strategies.

As a formidable baseline comparison method, MiniRAG is specifically referenced in performance assessments against TagRAG, especially for lightweight adaptations. Despite its strong performance, it is noted that MiniRAG has a significantly higher graph construction time compared to TagRAG, which is a point of consideration when evaluating its overall efficiency. Moreover, MiniRAG's capabilities in knowledge graph construction allow it to capture a vast array of entities while performing effectively with smaller computational models.

In summary, MiniRAG presents a robust approach to graph-based retrieval and inference tasks, although it faces challenges related to graph construction time, necessitating careful comparison with alternative methods like TagRAG.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ac038b8f5f47fa541303b546a0df1bf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d7629e55627c5114e5c8553304cfaf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ef51634d2a912725971ad5d52c5142d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b615900891f95591862c531adedc9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f24883bfa660df15d08e8b13fb36a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a666055a236002fef9bb78a46449b7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-914f521409f287f2603dab0bba5c0f95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ebd52158a59e9e9abf2431acd03979e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffda1de83dfb7a5a6814e4849f7c189e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583034</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
