    <node id="Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation">
      <data key="d0">Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation (GraphRAG) is a method that combines retrieval processes with graph structures to enhance multi-hop reasoning in question answering.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583035</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bridge-Guided Dual-Thought-based Retrieval">
      <data key="d0">Bridge-Guided Dual-Thought-based Retrieval</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Bridge-Guided Dual-Thought-based Retrieval (BDTR) integrates Dual-Thought-based Retrieval and Bridge-Guided Evidence Calibration to refine evidence in multi-hop question answering.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583035</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LLM">
      <data key="d0">LLM</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">LLM refers to large language models utilized for generating responses based on queries and context provided.&lt;SEP&gt;LLM, or Large Language Model, refers to advanced machine learning models designed for understanding and generating human language.&lt;SEP&gt;LLM refers to large language models that are utilized for various natural language processing tasks, including targeted graph retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;LLM refers to large language models, which can comprehend instructions and enhance knowledge retrieval efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;LLM refers to large language models used for complex tasks like text generation, question answering, and information retrieval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b568dd91e0d3a80a5dfbf3433e1123f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b88e564c6e5481a9f0d34cd7ae3cc0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ebd52158a59e9e9abf2431acd03979e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583035</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RAG System">
      <data key="d0">RAG System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The RAG system refers to a retrieval-augmented generation system designed to improve answer generation using document content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583035</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="KG">
      <data key="d0">KG</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">KG is a method for building an index between multiple documents, allowing for enhanced knowledge retrieval and reasoning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583036</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Naive RAG">
      <data key="d0">Naive RAG</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Naive RAG is a baseline RAG system that segments texts into chunks stored in a vector database using text embeddings.&lt;SEP&gt;Naive RAG is an early research paradigm of RAG that emphasizes a straightforward process involving indexing, retrieval, and generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Naive RAG is a retrieval-augmented generation framework that includes indexing, retrieval, and generation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Naive RAG is a simpler architecture compared to Modular RAG, characterized by fixed structures and a basic retrieval mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Naive RAG is a straightforward approach to retrieval-augmented generation that relies heavily on the user's original query.&lt;SEP&gt;Naive RAG is a baseline method compared against TagRAG in terms of winning rates in knowledge graph construction and reasoning scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0153506fe6cfb54fe11a5557e1a5a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2807be669ed8cdf9e947355ab6a13d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edb3902e4cb2b66ae3699b6d1a2451d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b88e564c6e5481a9f0d34cd7ae3cc0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555fe0d2d7e01e7cf8692d28ba90ccc7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583036</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Query">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Query</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Multi-Query is a technique that involves executing expanded queries in parallel to enrich the content and context of the original question.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583036</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sub-Query">
      <data key="d0">Sub-Query</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Sub-Query refers to the generation of necessary sub-questions to fully address and contextualize the original question.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583036</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chain-of-Verification (CoVe)">
      <data key="d0">Chain-of-Verification (CoVe)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">CoVe is a process where expanded queries are validated by LLM to reduce inaccuracies known as hallucinations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Query Rewrite">
      <data key="d0">Query Rewrite</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Query Rewrite involves prompting LLM to transform original queries into more optimal formats for retrieval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583037</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HyDE">
      <data key="d0">HyDE</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">HyDE is a method that generates hypothetical documents from input queries to retrieve relevant text chunks.&lt;SEP&gt;HyDE, or Hypothetical Document Embeddings, is a technique used to improve retrieval relevance by focusing on embedding similarities between generated answers and real documents.&lt;SEP&gt;HyDE is a query transformation technique that constructs hypothetical documents to answer the original query.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2807be669ed8cdf9e947355ab6a13d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Step-back Prompting">
      <data key="d0">Step-back Prompting</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Step-back Prompting is a method to abstract the original query into a high-level question for enhanced retrieval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Metadata Router">
      <data key="d0">Metadata Router</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Metadata Router is a routing approach that extracts keywords from queries to narrow down the search for relevant information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Semantic Router">
      <data key="d0">Semantic Router</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Semantic Router leverages the semantic information within a query to improve routing effectiveness in retrieval systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1643acfc11b9ce83e842d06ad4bc4c3d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583038</data>
