    <node id="Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)">
      <data key="d0">Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a paradigm designed to improve large language models by grounding generation in external evidence for question-answering tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) refers to systems that improve large language models by integrating external knowledge for more accurate responses.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG is a framework that combines user queries with relevant documents to generate coherent responses based on an external knowledge database.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) refers to a methodology in machine learning for efficient information retrieval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-84d742eb8f55bba51e586b51f2ebe7ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d6d9678ee09aab0dfe417365eafee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a18be2a653ce076549457febaf41543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2166023ef5af5223914f65a3580aa066</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583065</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
