    </node>
    <node id="Retrieval-Augmented Generation">
      <data key="d0">Retrieval-Augmented Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Retrieval-Augmented Generation is a methodology that enhances the capabilities of large language models by integrating external knowledge sources.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a framework that integrates retrieval systems with generative models to produce contextually relevant responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) refers to a methodology that combines retrieval techniques with generative models to improve answer generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a technology that enhances inputs to large language models by sourcing relevant information from external databases.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-Augmented Generation is a method that enhances large language models by integrating knowledge from external databases to improve the accuracy and credibility of generated content.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-augmented generation refers to techniques that improve generative models by incorporating retrieval processes to enhance output quality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-84d742eb8f55bba51e586b51f2ebe7ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e60306d296c9f4667ce0d438b79c6bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31769474f49786c5c06e27472659b8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50fab934716e3d9351f065107bc18294&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dc9263f77a3b5d565a77a808d2de587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555fe0d2d7e01e7cf8692d28ba90ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f402bb5d5231c590d516c203f0ed9166</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583066</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GPT">
      <data key="d0">GPT</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">GPT is a large language model that generates human-like text and is often used in various language processing tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba6c71d1ddc357fca61579af68e50fe0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583066</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LLMLingua">
      <data key="d0">LLMLingua</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">LLMLingua utilizes small language models to improve information extraction and facilitate comprehension by LLMs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583066</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PRCA">
      <data key="d0">PRCA</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">PRCA is a dataset-based method focused on document inference.&lt;SEP&gt;PRCA adds a contextual adapter to enhance performance for specific tasks in machine learning applications.&lt;SEP&gt;PRCA refers to a method that trains an information extractor to enhance the retrieval accuracy in language models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6323519fa42575408756a46a90ad82c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-269f5e6f28821bf79c7854694a47f38e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583066</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RECOMP">
      <data key="d0">RECOMP</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">RECOMP employs a training approach using contrastive learning to create an information condenser for better data handling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583066</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Filter-Reranker">
      <data key="d0">Filter-Reranker</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Filter-Reranker paradigm leverages both LLMs and SLMs to improve the relevance of the model's outputs by refining retrieval processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583067</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="SANTA Framework">
      <data key="d0">SANTA Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The SANTA framework implements a structured training regimen to effectively encapsulate structural and semantic aspects in language models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583067</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RA-DIT">
      <data key="d0">RA-DIT</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">RA-DIT aligns scoring functions between retrievers and generators using KL divergence for improved answer generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583067</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ITER-RETGEN">
      <data key="d0">ITER-RETGEN</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">ITER-RETGEN features a flow that iterates retrieval and reading processes for improved outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;ITER-RETGEN is an iterative method for Wikipedia text chunk inference.&lt;SEP&gt;ITER-RETGEN combines retrieval-enhanced generation with generation-enhanced retrieval to reproduce specific information effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6323519fa42575408756a46a90ad82c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Iterative Retrieval">
      <data key="d0">Iterative Retrieval</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Iterative retrieval refers to the process of repeatedly retrieving additional evidence to enhance reasoning and answer accuracy in complex queries.&lt;SEP&gt;Iterative retrieval is a strategy used in GraphRAG that involves retrieving information multiple times to enhance accuracy and recall.&lt;SEP&gt;Iterative retrieval is a process that repeatedly searches the knowledge base for improved information gathering and context enhancement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbcf5df5b02a500f3b2ea2c8ec7025cd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Large Language Models">
      <data key="d0">Large Language Models</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Large Language Models refer to advanced algorithms capable of understanding and generating human-like text but face challenges such as hallucination and outdated knowledge.&lt;SEP&gt;Large Language Models refer to advanced artificial intelligence systems, such as GPT, capable of understanding and generating human-like text.&lt;SEP&gt;Large Language Models (LLMs) are advanced computational models designed to generate and understand human language.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a666055a236002fef9bb78a46449b7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555fe0d2d7e01e7cf8692d28ba90ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f402bb5d5231c590d516c203f0ed9166</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="SLMs">
      <data key="d0">SLMs</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Small Language Models are simplified language processing models that are used in conjunction with LLMs for various applications in natural language understanding.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contrastive Learning">
      <data key="d0">Contrastive Learning</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Contrastive learning is a machine learning technique used to improve the accuracy and performance of models by distinguishing between similar and different data points.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1786160a84afa26e0b7e6e131ce199c3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583068</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="UltraDomain CS">
      <data key="d0">UltraDomain CS</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">UltraDomain CS is another dataset used for evaluating the performance of TagRAG.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d7629e55627c5114e5c8553304cfaf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583069</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="UltraDomain Legal">
      <data key="d0">UltraDomain Legal</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">UltraDomain Legal is one of the datasets utilized in the ablation study comparing TagRAG's performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d7629e55627c5114e5c8553304cfaf7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583069</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="UltraDomain Mix">
      <data key="d0">UltraDomain Mix</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">UltraDomain Mix is a dataset used in the analysis of TagRAG's capabilities and performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d7629e55627c5114e5c8553304cfaf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f24883bfa660df15d08e8b13fb36a4d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583069</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diversity">
      <data key="d0">Diversity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Diversity refers to the capability of TagRAG to leverage domain knowledge for broader information access in generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diversity measures the variety of questions and responses generated, indicating TagRAG's ability to produce varied and relevant outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Diversity indicates the variety of techniques and perspectives presented within the feature selection methods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d7629e55627c5114e5c8553304cfaf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0153506fe6cfb54fe11a5557e1a5a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aec7f8f39f2b2b14e58a248d55aa8ff6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583070</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Comprehensiveness">
      <data key="d0">Comprehensiveness</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Comprehensiveness is a measure used in the analysis of TagRAG performance across various datasets.&lt;SEP&gt;Comprehensiveness reflects the completeness and quality of the information generated by TagRAG, showing high winning rates against other methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Comprehensiveness refers to the overall extent and thoroughness of the feature selection methods discussed in the context of their effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d7629e55627c5114e5c8553304cfaf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0153506fe6cfb54fe11a5557e1a5a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aec7f8f39f2b2b14e58a248d55aa8ff6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583070</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-Hop QA">
      <data key="d0">Multi-Hop QA</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Multi-hop QA is a type of question-answering that requires linking multiple pieces of evidence to answer complex queries.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-hop QA refers to a type of question answering that requires connecting information from multiple sources or documents to answer complex questions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbcf5df5b02a500f3b2ea2c8ec7025cd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583070</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bridge Documents">
      <data key="d0">Bridge Documents</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bridge documents are intermediate facts that connect otherwise disjoint entities, crucial for answering multi-hop questions effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583070</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HotpotQA">
      <data key="d0">HotpotQA</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">HotpotQA is a multi-hop question answering dataset used to evaluate the effectiveness of iterative retrieval methods in GraphRAG.&lt;SEP&gt;HotpotQA is a widely used multi-hop QA benchmark utilized to evaluate the effectiveness of the proposed approach.&lt;SEP&gt;HotpotQA is a multi-hop question-answering dataset that includes specific question types like Bridge and Comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;HotpotQA is a specific version of Wikipedia Dump used for open-domain question-answering tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;HotpotQA is a multi-hop question answering dataset requiring models to retrieve information from multiple documents to answer questions.&lt;SEP&gt;HotpotQA is a dataset designed for multi-hop question answering, co-authored by Yang et al.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6beb5ec194d0b84b44b30e04fbf25a2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c698ed84457a758cb717d3a15350b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6323519fa42575408756a46a90ad82c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f188543fb58390e379ea6d2f1dc2ef58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe13b92a1c768e1d7f7a8b32dd7be5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db856360bc385f7452666f475b3048d0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583070</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="2WikiMultiHopQA">
      <data key="d0">2WikiMultiHopQA</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">2WikiMultiHopQA is a multi-hop question answering dataset included in the experiments to test the iterative retrieval framework.&lt;SEP&gt;2WikiMultiHopQA is another multi-hop QA benchmark leveraged for testing the approach's efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;2WikiMultiHopQA is a multi-hop question-answering dataset that contains four types of questions: Bridge+Comparison, Comparison, Compositional, and Inference.&lt;SEP&gt;2WikiMultiHopQA is a dataset that tests question answering systems on multi-hop questions sourced from Wikipedia.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c698ed84457a758cb717d3a15350b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f188543fb58390e379ea6d2f1dc2ef58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe13b92a1c768e1d7f7a8b32dd7be5d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583071</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MuSiQue">
      <data key="d0">MuSiQue</data>
      <data key="d1">dataset</data>
      <data key="d2">MuSiQue is another dataset for multi-hop question answering that assesses the performance of the iterative retrieval strategies in GraphRAG.&lt;SEP&gt;MuSiQue is a multi-hop QA benchmark used in the evaluation of the proposed retrieval methods.&lt;SEP&gt;MuSiQue is a dataset designed for multi-sentence question answering tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;MuSiQue is a method or system involved in the area of question answering.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c698ed84457a758cb717d3a15350b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abe51409947ebafac08b992d276558bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f188543fb58390e379ea6d2f1dc2ef58</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583071</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Exact Match">
      <data key="d0">Exact Match</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Exact Match is an evaluation metric used to assess the accuracy of answers in question answering tasks, often utilized in multi-hop QA evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583071</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="F1">
      <data key="d0">F1</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">F1 is a metric used in evaluating the performance of models by calculating the balance between precision and recall in question answering tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;F1 is a metric that measures the token-level overlap between predicted and gold answers, reflecting partial correctness in evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;F1 is a metric that measures token-level overlap between predicted and gold answers, providing a softer evaluation that captures partial correctness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7d04194f31f60d299ad968d7ef6e974f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbe13b92a1c768e1d7f7a8b32dd7be5d</data>
