    </node>
    <node id="Cultural Significance of Land Ownership">
      <data key="d0">Cultural Significance of Land Ownership</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cultural Significance of Land Ownership highlights the importance of land in indigenous cultures, influencing corporate strategies and collaborations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4dab3d7bf1cd6f56a1ccda1dd029330</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583109</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Role of Collaboration">
      <data key="d0">Role of Collaboration</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Role of Collaboration describes how collaboration is prioritized over competition between indigenous groups and corporations in the context of mergers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4dab3d7bf1cd6f56a1ccda1dd029330</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583109</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Legal and Regulatory Frameworks">
      <data key="d0">Legal and Regulatory Frameworks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal and Regulatory Frameworks address the laws that govern corporate mergers and the respect for indigenous rights during this process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4dab3d7bf1cd6f56a1ccda1dd029330</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583109</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RAG Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">RAG Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">RAG Evaluation refers to a framework for assessing the effectiveness of different responses to a query based on specific criteria such as comprehensiveness, diversity, and empowerment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4dab3d7bf1cd6f56a1ccda1dd029330</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583110</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Query Generation">
      <data key="d0">Query Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Query Generation outlines a method for identifying user roles and their objectives for creating queries based on a dataset description.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4dab3d7bf1cd6f56a1ccda1dd029330</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583110</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="UltraDomain CS Dataset">
      <data key="d0">UltraDomain CS Dataset</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">UltraDomain CS dataset is a collection of documents used to test the performance of various knowledge graph methods in incremental scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;The UltraDomain CS dataset is added to the knowledge graph constructed from the Mix dataset to demonstrate cross-domain capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d0153506fe6cfb54fe11a5557e1a5a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f24883bfa660df15d08e8b13fb36a4d</data>
