    </node>
    <node id="Hybrid Mode">
      <data key="d0">Hybrid Mode</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hybrid Mode is a variant of LightRAG that integrates both low-level and high-level retrieval methods for comprehensive data analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8df6d9b6dac5a8a1f205aa747dac043f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583170</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Retrieval Process">
      <data key="d0">Retrieval Process</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Retrieval Process is the series of operations involved in extracting information from datasets using defined methods like LightRAG and NaiveRAG.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval Process encompasses the series of steps involved in extracting relevant documents from data sources, including pre-processing and selection of models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8df6d9b6dac5a8a1f205aa747dac043f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-947ec822a759fcee4b9eb66e23cede0d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583171</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Semantic Graph">
      <data key="d0">Semantic Graph</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Semantic Graph is a structure that enhances the retrieval process by organizing information into a graph-based format for better query responses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8df6d9b6dac5a8a1f205aa747dac043f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583171</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NaiveRAG -High">
      <data key="d0">NaiveRAG -High</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">NaiveRAG -High is a variant of NaiveRAG that emphasizes high-level retrieval, resulting in a performance decline in various metrics due to its focus on specific information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8df6d9b6dac5a8a1f205aa747dac043f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583171</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NaiveRAG -Low">
      <data key="d0">NaiveRAG -Low</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">NaiveRAG -Low is a variant of NaiveRAG that prioritizes broader content capture but sacrifices detailed insight into specific entities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8df6d9b6dac5a8a1f205aa747dac043f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583172</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NaiveRAG -Origin">
      <data key="d0">NaiveRAG -Origin</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">NaiveRAG -Origin is a version of NaiveRAG that eliminates original text use during retrieval, showing notable performance in some datasets and contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8df6d9b6dac5a8a1f205aa747dac043f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583172</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prize-Collecting Steiner Tree (PCST)">
      <data key="d0">Prize-Collecting Steiner Tree (PCST)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Prize-Collecting Steiner Tree (PCST) is an optimization problem used in the context of targeted graph retrieval to enhance retrieval efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b568dd91e0d3a80a5dfbf3433e1123f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583172</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="SKR">
      <data key="d0">SKR</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">SKR is a dataset-based method for Wikipedia text chunk inference that adapts to different contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;SKR is a method that classifies questions as known or unknown, applying retrieval enhancement selectively to potentially improve answer accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b568dd91e0d3a80a5dfbf3433e1123f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6323519fa42575408756a46a90ad82c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583172</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GenRead">
      <data key="d0">GenRead</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">GenRead is a method for iterative inference with large language models.&lt;SEP&gt;GenRead is a method that replaces traditional retrieval mechanisms with an LLM generator to produce more accurate contextual answers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b568dd91e0d3a80a5dfbf3433e1123f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6323519fa42575408756a46a90ad82c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Selfmem">
      <data key="d0">Selfmem</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Selfmem is a method that iteratively creates an unbounded memory pool for enhancing generative model performance through retrieval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b568dd91e0d3a80a5dfbf3433e1123f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="DenseX">
      <data key="d0">DenseX</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">DenseX introduces the concept of using propositions as retrieval units to improve precision and relevance in data retrieval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b568dd91e0d3a80a5dfbf3433e1123f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583173</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Small2Big">
      <data key="d0">Small2Big</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Small2Big is a method that proposes using smaller sentences as retrieval units while providing larger contexts to enhance understanding.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b568dd91e0d3a80a5dfbf3433e1123f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583173</data>
