    <node id="Table 1">
      <data key="d0">Table 1</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 1 presents EM and F1 performance across multi-hop QA datasets, highlighting the results ranked first and second for various frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 1 presents the win rates of LightRAG against various baselines across four datasets and evaluation dimensions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da2807be669ed8cdf9e947355ab6a13d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583264</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Frameworks">
      <data key="d0">Frameworks</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Frameworks refer to the systems used in the evaluation of multi-hop QA datasets such as Original, IRCOT, GCOT, TOG, IRGS, and Our.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583264</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Table 2">
      <data key="d0">Table 2</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Table 2 shows results on the Single-Hop dataset PopQA measured with different methods including GraphRAG backbones.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 2 presents the results of the evaluation comparing model performance metrics in terms of cost and adaptability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dc9263f77a3b5d565a77a808d2de587</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583264</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GraphRAG Variants">
      <data key="d0">GraphRAG Variants</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">GraphRAG variants include HippoRAG2, RAPTOR, GFM-RAG, and GraphRAG, each representing different retrieval paradigms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583264</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Implementation and Evaluation Metrics">
      <data key="d0">Implementation and Evaluation Metrics</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Implementation and Evaluation Metrics refers to the methods used for adopting the official codebases and metrics like Exact Match (EM) and F1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583265</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multi-hop QA Datasets">
      <data key="d0">Multi-hop QA Datasets</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Multi-hop QA datasets are collections of questions that require reasoning over multiple pieces of information to produce an answer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583265</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Our">
      <data key="d0">Our</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Our is a term used in the context of various frameworks and metrics discussed in relation to performance evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a054701fac93a0f7901f4619ad32bdd</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583265</data>
