    <node id="Naive RAG (Gao et al., 2023)">
      <data key="d0">Naive RAG (Gao et al., 2023)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Naive RAG, established by Gao et al. in 2023, serves as a standard baseline in existing RAG systems that segments raw texts into chunks and utilizes text embeddings for storage and retrieval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da2807be669ed8cdf9e947355ab6a13d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583321</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RQ-RAG (Chan et al., 2024)">
      <data key="d0">RQ-RAG (Chan et al., 2024)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">RQ-RAG, introduced by Chan et al. in 2024, enhances search accuracy through the use of LLM to create multiple sub-queries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da2807be669ed8cdf9e947355ab6a13d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583321</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HyDE (Gao et al., 2022)">
      <data key="d0">HyDE (Gao et al., 2022)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">HyDE, developed by Gao et al. in 2022, generates a hypothetical document from an input query to facilitate text chunk retrieval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da2807be669ed8cdf9e947355ab6a13d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583321</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GraphRAG (Edge et al., 2024)">
      <data key="d0">GraphRAG (Edge et al., 2024)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">GraphRAG is a graph-enhanced RAG system introduced by Edge et al. in 2024 that extracts entities and relationships from text.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da2807be669ed8cdf9e947355ab6a13d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583322</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Modular RAG">
      <data key="d0">Modular RAG</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Modular RAG is a variant of RAG designed to be cost-effective while addressing specific shortcomings of Naive RAG.&lt;SEP&gt;Modular RAG is a component of the RAG framework that emphasizes a modular approach to retrieving and generating information, contributing to the flexibility and adaptability of language models.&lt;SEP&gt;Modular RAG further develops the RAG frameworks, providing greater flexibility and adaptability in processing information.&lt;SEP&gt;Modular RAG is an advanced architecture that enhances adaptability and integrates diverse strategies for improving retrieval and processing capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edb3902e4cb2b66ae3699b6d1a2451d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b88e564c6e5481a9f0d34cd7ae3cc0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555fe0d2d7e01e7cf8692d28ba90ccc7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583322</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Search Module">
      <data key="d0">Search Module</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Search Module aids in performing similarity searches across various data sources, improving the retrieval process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583322</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Memory Module">
      <data key="d0">Memory Module</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Memory Module leverages LLM’s memory to guide retrieval, creating a flexible memory pool for improved information alignment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583322</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Predict Module">
      <data key="d0">Predict Module</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Predict Module generates context directly through LLM to reduce redundancy and enhance relevance in retrieved information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583322</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Task Adapter Module">
      <data key="d0">Task Adapter Module</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Task Adapter Module customizes RAG for various tasks, automating prompt retrieval for better performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583322</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rewrite-Retrieve-Read Model">
      <data key="d0">Rewrite-Retrieve-Read Model</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Rewrite-Retrieve-Read Model refines retrieval queries using a rewriting module and feedback mechanisms from the LLM.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583323</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Demonstrate-Search-Predict Framework">
      <data key="d0">Demonstrate-Search-Predict Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Demonstrate-Search-Predict Framework illustrates a method of using module outputs to enhance functionality across the Modular RAG architecture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583323</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fine-tuning">
      <data key="d0">Fine-tuning</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fine-tuning is a method that involves adapting models over time for specific tasks, contrasting with RAG's tailored retrieval approach.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583323</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Advanced RAG">
      <data key="d0">Advanced RAG</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Advanced RAG builds upon Naive RAG by addressing limitations, integrating more complex retrieval and generation techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Advanced RAG is a sophisticated model within the Retrieval-Augmented Generation framework that aims to provide enhanced capabilities for knowledge retrieval and integration.&lt;SEP&gt;Advanced RAG is an improved version of Naive RAG that enhances retrieval quality through specific strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Advanced RAG is a more refined retrieval architecture that builds upon the principles of basic RAG approaches.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb0fa3c7f17705ec4d14e2eea4192a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edb3902e4cb2b66ae3699b6d1a2451d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b88e564c6e5481a9f0d34cd7ae3cc0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-555fe0d2d7e01e7cf8692d28ba90ccc7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583323</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Statistics of Knowledge Graph Construction">
      <data key="d0">Statistics of Knowledge Graph Construction</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Statistics reported provide data on the number of entities and relationships constructed by various methods of knowledge graph construction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f24883bfa660df15d08e8b13fb36a4d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583323</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cross-domain Incremental Analysis">
      <data key="d0">Cross-domain Incremental Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Cross-domain incremental analysis refers to the evaluation of knowledge graph methods on different datasets to determine their effectiveness in using new data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f24883bfa660df15d08e8b13fb36a4d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583323</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
