    <node id="FG-RAG">
      <data key="d0">FG-RAG</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">FG-RAG is another method focused on improving the efficiency of inference in knowledge graph systems.&lt;SEP&gt;FG-RAG is a method introduced by Hong et al. in 2025 that improves response specificity with query-level fine-grained summarization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a666055a236002fef9bb78a46449b7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-914f521409f287f2603dab0bba5c0f95</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583343</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Documents Knowledge Graph">
      <data key="d0">Documents Knowledge Graph</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Documents Knowledge Graph refers to the structured representation of knowledge extracted from documents, facilitating information retrieval and understanding.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a666055a236002fef9bb78a46449b7a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583343</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Entity Relation Extraction">
      <data key="d0">Entity Relation Extraction</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Entity Relation Extraction is a method for identifying and categorizing entities and their relationships within documents for better information processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a666055a236002fef9bb78a46449b7a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583343</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Community Summarization">
      <data key="d0">Community Summarization</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Community Summarization is a process of generating concise summaries from grouped information within a knowledge community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a666055a236002fef9bb78a46449b7a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583344</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Evaluation Methods">
      <data key="d0">Evaluation Methods</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Evaluation methods refer to the assessment frameworks used to gauge the effectiveness of RAG processes and their outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-edb3902e4cb2b66ae3699b6d1a2451d1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583344</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ChatGPT">
      <data key="d0">ChatGPT</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">ChatGPT is a widely discussed large language model that relies on pre-training data to respond to user queries but requires RAG to provide up-to-date information.&lt;SEP&gt;ChatGPT is an AI chatbot that has contributed to the popularity of tools like LangChain and LLamaIndex and is linked to the advancement of RAG technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;ChatGPT is an AI language model that has triggered the popularity of tools like LangChain and LLamaIndex by enhancing RAG capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-edb3902e4cb2b66ae3699b6d1a2451d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4eee49b38d4fdcc5a4814bf5fc35e1dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99720e11d80a6f27e39053158f697be5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583344</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Retrieval">
      <data key="d0">Retrieval</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Retrieval is a core component of the RAG methodology that focuses on sourcing relevant information to enhance output generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-edb3902e4cb2b66ae3699b6d1a2451d1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583344</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Generation">
      <data key="d0">Generation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Generation is the process within the RAG framework where the retrieved information is used by LLMs to form coherent responses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-edb3902e4cb2b66ae3699b6d1a2451d1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780583344</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Augmentation">
      <data key="d0">Augmentation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Augmentation refers to the methods and techniques that enhance the initial raw outputs generated by LLMs, integrating additional data sources or processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-edb3902e4cb2b66ae3699b6d1a2451d1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
